<br clear=all style='mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always'>

<h1>CHAPTER 10: ALGORITHMS AND MATHEMATICAL FORMULATIONS</h1>
<h2>10.1 Weighted Coverage Formula (SRS Section 6.3)</h2>
<p>In recruitment evaluation, required skills carry different degrees of importance. Let $w_i \in [1.0, 5.0]$ represent the importance weight of required skill $i$ (where $5.0$ represents a mandatory core skill and $1.0$ represents a nice-to-have skill). Let $c_i \in \{1.0, 0.5, 0.0\}$ represent the assessed student competency level.</p>
<div class="box">
  Coverage_weighted (%) = [ Sum(w_i * c_i) / Sum(w_i) ] * 100<br>
  Gap_weighted (%) = 100 - Coverage_weighted (%)
</div>

<h2>10.2 Basic Unweighted Coverage Formula</h2>
<div class="box">
  Coverage_unweighted (%) = [ Count of Required Skills Covered / Total Required Skills ] * 100<br>
  Gap_unweighted (%) = 100 - Coverage_unweighted (%)
</div>

<h2>10.3 Token-Boundary Regular Expression Extraction</h2>
<div class="box">
  P(t) = RegEx( (?&lt;!\w) + escape(t) + (?!\w), IGNORECASE )<br>
  Confidence(s_j) = min(0.98, 0.85 + 0.04 * (frequency - 1))
</div>

<br clear=all style='mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always'>

