<h1>CHAPTER 13: EMPIRICAL MODEL EVALUATION RESULTS</h1>
<p>The model evaluation benchmark was executed on the ground-truth labeled benchmark dataset containing 30 verified skill annotations across 6 authentic academic syllabi and job descriptions:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Model Architecture</th><th>TP</th><th>FP</th><th>FN</th><th>Precision</th><th>Recall</th><th>F1 Score</th><th>Mapping Precision</th><th>Gap Coverage</th></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Proposed Contextual NLP Pipeline</strong></td><td><strong>26</strong></td><td><strong>1</strong></td><td><strong>4</strong></td><td><strong>0.9630 (96.3%)</strong></td><td><strong>0.8667 (86.7%)</strong></td><td><strong>0.9123 (91.2%)</strong></td><td><strong>0.9400 (94.0%)</strong></td><td><strong>0.9200 (92.0%)</strong></td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Naive Substring Keyword Baseline</strong></td><td>18</td><td>3</td><td>12</td><td>0.8571 (85.7%)</td><td>0.6000 (60.0%)</td><td>0.7059 (70.6%)</td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
  <tr><td><strong>Empirical Improvement (&Delta;)</strong></td><td><strong>+8</strong></td><td><strong>-2</strong></td><td><strong>-8</strong></td><td><strong>+10.6%</strong></td><td><strong>+26.7%</strong></td><td><strong>+20.6%</strong></td><td>—</td><td>—</td></tr>
</table>

<br clear=all style='mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always'>

<h1>CHAPTER 14: CONCLUSION AND FUTURE SCOPE</h1>
<p>The <strong>Academia–Industry Skill Mapping and Placement Portal</strong> developed for <strong>Smart India Hackathon 2026 (Problem Statement ID: SIH26044 &middot; Group G29)</strong> establishes a robust, mathematically rigorous, and empirically validated solution to the widening divide between higher education curricula and industry employment expectations.</p>
<p>By integrating contextual NLP skill extraction, canonical taxonomy normalization, importance-weighted coverage formulations ($w_i \cdot c_i$), gap-targeted learning pathways, and cohort-level analytics, the system provides actionable value to all five key stakeholders. Tested across twelve formal test scenarios and evaluated against a ground-truth benchmark achieving an <strong>F1 score of 0.9123 (+20.6% gain over baseline)</strong>, the portal represents a production-ready blueprint for data-driven academic curriculum enhancement and placement readiness assessment.</p>

